Hi,

picker@ee.ualberta.ca (Derek Pickering) writes:
>1) How high can a weapon be enchanted?
>   (ie: if I used 3 blessed scrolls of enchant weapon on a sword,
>    would it be enchanted to about +9 or would something nasty happen?)

Everything over +5 has a chance that your weapon/armour evaporates.

>2) Could I wish for a "blessed magic lamp" and get it?
>   Do they always give wishes?

You would get it, but you would not get any wishes from it.  As far as
I know, there is NO way to get more wish-items from a wish.

>3) How many times can a WoW be charged from a blessed scroll of C and
>   what is the max number of charges a WoW has?

You can charge it ONCE.  The second charge will destroy the WoW.
The standard procedure with a WoW is to wish for a blessed scroll of
charging first, then get two useful items from the other wishes.
Recharge the WoW, get more items.  When the WoW seems to be empty, keep
zapping it.  You will finally wrest one more wish from the wand, and it
will evaporate.

4) Can a magic marker be recharged a zillion times?
>5) What items are ESSENTIAL for finishing the game? (I've Finally got
>   a shot at it!)

The Amulet of Yendor.  You offer it on a co-aligned altar in the endlevel.

>6) How can one open the castle drawbridge without an insterment, a wand
>   of striking, or a spell of knock(or something similar)  I DO have a lock
>   pick and a pick axe, will they help?

How to get into the castle:
(1) get an instrument and play master-mind
(2) knock the drawbridge down 
(3) use a ring or boot of levitation and fly over the moat to get to 
    the back-entrance

